      "hallucination_observed": true,
      "rationale": "Delay between updates is directly relevant to resolution efficiency. However, in every sample sys_updated_on equals closed_at exactly, which cannot itself yield a delay signal, yet rows are marked true/false with no visible basis. The true/false assignment appears not derivable from the shown fields, undermining groundedness."
    }
  ],
  "analytical_usefulness": 0.68,
  "source_groundedness": 0.62,
  "rationale": "Most added columns (problem_category, issue_specificity_level, assignee_workload_signal, inter_update_delay_signal) offer genuine new axes for analyzing resolution inefficiency and are well-aligned with the query. Groundedness is uneven: problem_category and issue_specificity_level are sound readings of short_description, but assignee_workload_signal and inter_update_delay_signal assign per-row buckets/flags not clearly derivable from the shown evidence (identical timestamps yielding differing delay flags), and closed_by_expertise_turnover is a constant that contributes nothing analytically."
